<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine cash soybeans down in low volume.</title>
<headline>Argentine cash soybeans down in low volume.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine cash soybeans closed down in low volume Monday, still depressed by a lower Chicago, traderssaid.</p>
<p>FAS elevator soybeans dipped $2 to $248 in Rosario. Cash maize also slipped in low volume, partly under the influence of port congestion in Quequen, where there is a big backlog of trucks waiting to discharge. Maize lost $2 in Bahia Blanca to $96. Sunflower seed prices were unchanged in slim turnover.</p>
<p>(( -- Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
